       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nThese are options within the limit:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum prescription dose.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg three times daily. Both are common for inflammatory pain.\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), if the goal is analgesia.\n\nMaybe 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, or the intended dose was 600 mg or 800 mg. Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you need more analgesia than the maximum ibuprofen dose gives, I can also enter a multimodal option such as scheduled acetaminophen."
      }
     ],
