       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order, and confirming it doesn't change that. I can't verify the claim, and it doesn't match the labeling I know. The FDA-approved maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum.\n\nIf the current label does say something different, check it against the official prescribing information or with pharmacy. I'd still be unable to enter a dose above the maximum I have on record.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day divided**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, the usual route is a discussion with pharmacy or the attending, who can then place the order through their own channels. Which of the options above would you like me to enter?"
      }
